		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Organization and Nature of Business&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;BBT Trans-Union Interstate Pipeline, LP ("Trans-Union") is a Delaware limited partnership, which consists of a 99% limited partner ("LP") interest and a 1% general partner ("GP") interest. Since December 10, 2019, both the GP interest and the LP interest have been held by wholly owned subsidiaries of Black Bear Transmission Holdco, LLC ("BBT").&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Trans-Union owns a 42-mile, 30-inch natural gas interstate pipeline which transports natural gas from upstream interconnections in Sharon, Louisiana in Claiborne Parish to downstream interconnections near El Dorado, Arkansas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Trans-Union operates in multiple states and is engaged in interstate commerce and, as such, is subject to the rules, regulations and accounting procedures of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, ("FERC") pursuant to the Natural Gas Act of 1938 and the Natural Gas Policy Act of 1978. On November 12, 2025, Trans-Union's parent company sold Trans-Union and various other subsidiaries to Enstor Pipeline Holdings, LLC, an affiliate of Enstor Gas, LLC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements prescribed by the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America ("GAAP").&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;The most significant difference between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein is that the FERC does not permit "push down" accounting for acquisitions of an operating company by a parent company. Additionally, the FERC requires that the Company reflect a hypothetical provision for federal and state income taxes and related balance sheet accounts, even though it is not subject to such taxes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with FERC regulations requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of certain assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of expenses and/or revenues during the year. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cash Management Program&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;We had no cash or cash equivalents as of December 31, 2025, or 2024, as all cash is managed collectively by BBT on a centralized basis and is advanced between its affiliates as needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Special Deposits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Cash and cash equivalents that are restricted as to withdrawal or under the terms of certain contractual agreements are recorded as Special Deposits on the accompanying balance sheet. We place our cash and cash equivalents with high credit quality financial institutions. At times, our cash and cash equivalents may be uninsured or in deposit accounts that exceed the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation insurance limit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Transportation and Exchange Gas Imbalances&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;In the course of providing transportation services, natural gas pipelines may receive different quantities of gas from shippers than the quantities delivered on behalf of those shippers. These transactions result in transportation and exchange gas imbalances. Such shipper imbalances are recorded as Regulatory Assets or Regulatory Liabilities in the accompanying balance sheet using the posted index prices of the applicable approved tariffs, which approximate market rates. These imbalances are required to be resolved within a specified period of time or when certain quantity thresholds are met. Resolution can be through imbalance trading with other shippers or by utilizing the cash out procedures specified in the tariff. Exchange imbalances are settled with other pipelines through the cashout procedures in their tariffs and recorded to the statement of income as Operating Expenses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Trans-Union establishes provisions for current expected credit losses on accounts receivable, when we determine that we will not collect all or part of an outstanding balance. Such determination is made at the time the revenue is recognized. The balance of allowance for credit losses was zero as of December 31, 2025, and 2024. For the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024, we did not have any bad debt expense.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Utility Plant&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

