			&lt;p style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; margin: 0pt; text-align: center;"&gt;Net Utility Plant&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 1%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 1%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-left: 0pt; border-bottom: 3px double rgb(0, 0, 0);"&gt;$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 15%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-left: 0pt; border-bottom: 3px double rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: right;"&gt;9,890,531&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 1%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; padding-bottom: 3px; margin-left: 0pt; border-bottom: 3px double black;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 1%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; border-bottom: 3px double black;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 1%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-left: 0pt; border-bottom: 3px double rgb(0, 0, 0);"&gt;$&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 15%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-left: 0pt; border-bottom: 3px double rgb(0, 0, 0); text-align: right;"&gt;11,235,444&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 1%; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; padding-bottom: 3px; margin-left: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Transfers from Construction Work in Progress to Utility plant totaled $0 for both, December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Trans-Union is not subject to federal or state income taxes; however, the related tax impacts of its operations are reported on the tax returns of Trans-Union's sole member. For ratemaking purposes, Trans-Union is treated as if it were a corporation that would require comprehensive income tax procedures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;In accordance with FERC requirements, the accompanying financial statements include a hypothetical provision for federal and state income taxes as if Trans-Union were a taxable entity following the guidance outlined in the Accounting Standards Codification 740, Income Taxes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Allocation of Salary and Overhead Expense Policy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Effective January 1, 2021, BBT began applying the Modified Massachusetts Formula ("MMF") method based on a proportionate percentage of revenue, payroll costs and plant assets, which management believes to be reasonable in the circumstances. Such allocations totaled $1,080,266 and $797,202 under the MMF method for the years ended December 31,2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Our interstate transportation results are determined primarily by the amount of capacity customers reserve as well as the actual volume of natural gas that flows through the transportation pipeline. Under transportation contracts, our customers are charged (i) a firm transportation fee, which is a fixed fee regardless of how much natural gas is transported, (ii) an annual charge adjustment unit fee, which is based on every unit of volume of natural gas delivered utilizing rates as determined by the FERC, (iii) an interruptible transportation fee if applicable, or (iv) a combination of the three.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Revenue is recognized over the service period specified in the contract as the services are rendered using a time-based (passage of time) or units-based (units of service transferred) method for measuring provision of the services. Progress towards satisfying our performance obligation is based on the firm or interruptible nature of the promised service and the terms and conditions of the contract. Payment is generally received from the customer in the month of service or the month following the service. Contracts with customers generally are a combination of month-to-month and multi-year agreements. Revenues related to these services provided but not yet billed are estimated each month. These estimates are generally based on contract data, regulatory information, and preliminary throughput and allocation measurements. Final bills for the current month are billed and collected in the following month.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;In 2014, the Financial Accounting Standards Board ("FASB") issued Accounting Standards Update ("ASU") No. 2014-09, "Revenue from Contracts with Customers (Topic 606)", which supersedes most of the existing revenue recognition requirements in GAAP and requires entities to recognize revenue at an amount that reflects the consideration to which an entity expects to be entitled in exchange for transferring goods or services to a customer. It also requires significantly expanded disclosures regarding the qualitative and quantitative information of an entity's nature, amount, timing and uncertainty of revenue and cash flows arising from contracts with customers. We are not adopting the comprehensive disclosure requirements of ASC 606, as the Company is not required to do so for FERC reporting purposes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Trans-Union follows FERC Order No. 631, Accounting, Financial Reporting and Rate Filing Requirements for Asset Retirement Obligations ("ARO"), which addresses accounting and reporting for asset retirement obligations associated with the retirement of long-lived tangible assets. Order No. 631 requires entities to record the fair value of a liability for the retirement obligation in the period in which the liability is incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. The associated retirement cost is capitalized as part of the carrying value of the underlying asset and is subsequently depreciated over the underlying asset's useful life. After initial recognition, the ARO is revised to reflect the passage of time through accretion and for changes in the estimate amount or timing of cash flows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Legal obligations exist for certain of Trans-Union's pipeline transmission assets. Trans-Union has not recognized the related ARO's as of December 31, 2025, or 2024 as the ultimate retirement dates of the underlying assets are uncertain and the related retirement costs are not estimable. An ARO will be recognized in the period in which sufficient information exists to reasonably estimate the settlement dates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fair Value Measurement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;We use fair value to measure certain of the assets and liabilities in our financial statements. Fair value is the amount that would be received to sell an asset or paid to transfer a liability in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date (i.e., the exit price). We categorize the fair value of our financial assets and liabilities according to the hierarchy established by the Financial Accounting Standards Board (the "FASB"), which prioritizes the inputs to valuation techniques used to measure fair value. We also consider counterparty credit risk in our assessment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Hierarchy levels 1, 2, or 3 are terms for the priority of inputs to valuation techniques used to measure fair value. The three levels of the fair value hierarchy are described as follows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&#9679;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Level 1 - Quoted market prices in active markets for identical assets or liabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&#9679;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Level 2 - Inputs other than Level 1 inputs that are either directly or indirectly observable.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&#9679;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;Level 3 - Unobservable inputs developed using estimates and assumptions developed by management, which reflect those that a market participant would use.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, we had four customers which individually accounted for 43%, 21%, 21%, 15% of total accounts receivable. If we were to lose any or all four customers, our results of operations and financial position could be materially adversely affected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;For the year ended December 31, 2025, we had four customers which individually accounted for 39%, 24%, 22%, and 15% of our revenues. For the year ended December 31, 2024, we had four customers which individually accounted for 40%, 24%, 21%, and 15%, respectively, of our revenues.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:10pt;font-variant:normal;margin:0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Parties&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;For the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024, no transportation revenues were earned from related parties. All transportation revenues earned were at rates pursuant to the existing tariffs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Regulatory Assets and Regulatory Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;Regulatory Assets and Regulatory Liabilities include shipper imbalances, OBA imbalances, lost and unaccounted for gas ("LAUF"), Annual Charge Assessments ("ACA") and excess/grossed up tax adjustments.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;At December 31, 2025, and 2024, Regulatory Assets totaled $102,181 and $121,424, respectively. At December 31, 2025, and 2024, Regulatory Liabilities totaled $30,896,228 and $25,203,425, respectively. Trans-Union is reviewing the accumulated over-recovery of gas reflected in its Lost and Unaccounted For Regulatory Liability as recorded in Account 254. The ongoing review includes determining the root-cause of the over-recovery in order to evaluate the proper future disposition of the accumulated Lost and Unaccounted For from Account 254.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="width: 100%; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr style="vertical-align: top;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: 18pt;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;6.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="width: auto;"&gt;
			&lt;p style="margin: 0pt; text-align: left; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
		&lt;/tr&gt;
	
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;A reconciliation of TransUnion's provision for income taxes calculated at the federal statutory rate to the actual income tax provision recorded for the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024 is as follows:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="finTable" style="margin-right: 2.5%; margin-left: 2.5%; width: 95%; font-size: 10pt; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; text-indent: 0px;"&gt;
	
		&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr class="finHeading" style="vertical-align: bottom; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;
			&lt;td style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td colspan="2" style="text-align: center; font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin-left: 0pt; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(0, 0, 0);"&gt;
			&lt;p style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; font-variant: normal; text-align: center; margin: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;2025&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;td style="font-family: &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; padding-bottom: 1px; border-bottom: 1px solid black;"&gt;&amp;#xa0;&lt;/td&gt;
